# {{name}}

An Ananke streaming conversational agent scaffolded with `nnke new chatbox`.  
Exposes a Minimal API with SSE streaming via `StreamingChatWorkflow`.

## Run it

```bash
dotnet run
```

Then in another terminal:

```bash
# Single JSON response
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:5000/chat \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{"message":"What can Ananke do?"}'

# Streaming (Server-Sent Events)
curl -N -X POST http://localhost:5000/chat/stream \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{"message":"Tell me about agentic workflows."}'
```

No API key required yet — `SimulatedStreamingModel` streams word-by-word so you
can see the SSE transport in action immediately.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{name}}.csproj` | ASP.NET Minimal API — references `Ananke.Orchestration` + `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` |
| `Program.cs` | API endpoints + `SimulatedStreamingModel` (swap for real provider when ready) |
| `secrets.json` | API key placeholder — never commit this |

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/chat` | Full JSON response `{"reply":"..."}` |
| `POST` | `/chat/stream` | SSE stream of text deltas, ends with `data: [DONE]` |

## Switch to a real LLM provider

See the commented-out provider blocks at the top of `Program.cs`:

```bash
# OpenAI
dotnet add package Ananke.Orchestration.OpenAI

# Anthropic
dotnet add package Ananke.Orchestration.Anthropic
```

Then update `secrets.json`:
```json
{ "OpenAI": { "ApiKey": "sk-..." } }
```

